---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Cascadia Systems">
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="hero-topo section bg-gradient-to-b from-dark-bg via-dark-surface to-dark-bg">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
        <h1 class="mb-8 text-center text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl">
          The workflow your team does <span class="text-gradient">by hand</span>
        </h1>
        <div class="mb-8 border-l-4 border-accent-blue bg-dark-surface/50 p-6 text-lg leading-relaxed">
          <p class="text-text-primary">
            <strong>Cascadia Systems puts a senior engineer inside your organization. In 30 days,
            the manual process costing you the most staff time runs itself, with an audit trail
            and a runbook your team can keep.</strong>
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-4 text-center text-lg text-text-secondary">
          <p>
            Intake, reconciliation, reporting, re-keying between two systems. Every organization
            has one process that eats a person's week. We map the five worst, automate the worst
            one, and leave you a plan for the rest.
          </p>
          <p>
            Fixed price. One engineer, start to finish. Your data stays in your systems.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-10 flex flex-col items-center justify-center gap-4 sm:flex-row">
          <a href="/services/" class="btn btn-primary">The 30-Day Diagnostic</a>
          <a href="/contact/" class="btn btn-secondary">Book a 30-minute call</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- How it works -->
  <section class="section border-t border-dark-border">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <h2 class="mb-12 text-center text-3xl font-bold sm:text-4xl">Thirty Days, Three Deliverables</h2>
      <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
        <div class="card">
          <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold text-accent-blue">1 · Map</h3>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            Interviews with the people who do the work. A map of your five costliest manual
            workflows: who does what, hours per month, where errors and delays enter, and what
            each one costs.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold text-accent-cyan">2 · Automate</h3>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            The workflow with the best ratio of pain to effort, built and running in production.
            Audit log, error handling, a runbook, and a training session. Not a prototype.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold text-accent-green">3 · Plan</h3>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            A 12-month roadmap: what to automate next and in what order, what to build versus
            buy, what it costs, and where AI genuinely helps versus where a spreadsheet is the
            right answer.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-10 text-center">
        <a href="/services/" class="btn btn-secondary">Full service details</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Who it's for -->
  <section class="section bg-dark-surface">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl">
        <h2 class="mb-8 text-3xl font-bold">Built for Organizations Like Yours</h2>
        <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
          <div class="card">
            <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold text-text-primary">Who calls us</h3>
            <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
              Clinics and healthcare groups, credit unions, property managers, logistics
              operators, professional firms, and nonprofits with a few hundred to a few thousand
              people served, a small team doing too much by hand, and a board asking what the
              plan for AI is.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold text-text-primary">What we have built</h3>
            <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
              Daily data pipelines and CRM integrations for a 41,000-member statewide
              organization. Document extraction that turns scanned applications into records.
              Automated financial reporting across 216 school districts. Event platforms,
              ServiceDesk automation, and reconciliation tools that caught what upstream vendors
              missed.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Data handling -->
  <section class="section border-t border-dark-border">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl">
        <h2 class="mb-12 text-center text-3xl font-bold sm:text-4xl">Your Data Stays in Your Systems</h2>
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
          <p>
            We work through read-only access first, and write access only for the workflow
            being automated. Sensitive processing runs in your environment or on
            infrastructure we own and control, with no third-party model provider involved.
          </p>
          <p>
            Where a hosted AI model is the right tool, it is a provider under a signed
            data-processing agreement with no training on your data. Every engagement ships
            with a written data-handling sheet, and everything we build is yours.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="section bg-dark-surface">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl text-center">
        <h2 class="mb-6 text-3xl font-bold sm:text-4xl">Start With a Call</h2>
        <p class="mb-8 text-text-secondary">
          Thirty minutes. Tell us the process that eats the most time. If a spreadsheet would
          fix it, we will say so on the call.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-col items-center justify-center gap-4 sm:flex-row">
          <a href="/contact/" class="btn btn-primary">Book a call</a>
          <a href="/about/" class="btn btn-secondary">Who does the work</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
